          }
        ],
        "comments": [
          {
            "paragraph_index": 2,
            "comment": ""
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 4,
            "comment": "Dissolve components except NaHCO3, Vitamin solution, Thiamine solution, Vitamin B12 solution, sodium lactate and Na2S・9H2O in 900 ml distilled water and adjust pH to 7.0. Bring to a boil and cool down under a N2--CO2 (4:1, v/v) gas stream. Distribute the medium into culture vessels (e.g., 9 ml of the medium in Hungate tubes) under a N2--CO2 (4:1, v/v) gas mixture, seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave. Separately autoclave 0.2 M sodium lactate under a N2 atmosphere. After cooling, add 1/9 volume of the sodium lactate solution, and filter--sterilized 8% NaHCO3 solution, Vitamin solution, Thiamine solution and Vitamin B12 solution tothe medium. Readjust pH to 7.0, if necessary. Prior to use, reduce the medium with Na2S・9H2O (3% solution, autoclaved and stocked under N2)."
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 5,
            "comment": ""
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 6,
            "comment": "Use JCM Medium No. [462] without Na2S・9H2O, and with 20 mM sodium acetate and 30 mM ferric citrate instead of sodium lactate. Reduce the medium with 0.5 g/L L--cysteine・HCl (5% solution, autoclaved and stored under N2)."
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 7,
            "comment": ""
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 9,
            "comment": ""
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 11,
            "comment": ""
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 13,
            "comment": ""
          }
        ],
