        "comments": [
          {
            "paragraph_index": 2,
            "comment": ""
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 4,
            "comment": "First dissolve iron(III) citrate in 800 ml distilled water and adjust pH to 7.0 with 10 N NaOH. Then, add the remaining minerals, bring volume to 970 ml and autoclave under a N2 atmosphere. Add aseptically and anaerobicallythe following filter--sterilized solutions:"
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 6,
            "comment": "Distribute the medium into sterile culture vessels (e.g., 50 ml per 120 mlbottle) under a N2--CO2 (4:1, v/v) gas mixture, and seal with sterile butylrubber stoppers. Then add per 50 ml the following solutions from anaerobic stocks:"
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 7,
            "comment": ""
          },
          {
            "paragraph_index": 9,
            "comment": "Check the final pH of the medium to be around 7.0."
          }
        ],
